  "owned_d": "Owned making is LEATHER GOODS AND FOOTWEAR (plus leather supply), not ready-to-wear. Gucci ArtLab, Scandicci (Florence), opened April 2018: leather goods (bags, luggage, SLG, belts) and footwear development/production, press quoting Gucci CEO; Wikipedia describes it as where leather goods, footwear, hardware and packaging are developed and tested. Tanneries: Gucci took 100% of Colonna Group (Marbella Pellami, Conceria 800, Falco Pellami, Santa Croce sull'Arno) Nov 2024; Kering also owns Caravel (Tuscany) and France Croco (Normandy) tanneries. Ready-to-wear: the only owned RTW site found is Kering's Novara complex (Via Belletti 4), described by its architects as 'offices and prototype making department' (~2,200 sq m labs) — prototyping, not production evidence. No owned RTW/knit production facility found; Gucci says its supply chain involves ~4,200 direct and sub-suppliers (WWD).",
